[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885920971","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962#issuecomment-4885920971","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120962","id":4885920971,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIzk8yw","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T11:45:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T11:45:41Z","body":"cc @Alex2782 @Kazox61 ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885920971/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886965206","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962#issuecomment-4886965206","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120962","id":4886965206,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0kr1g","user":{"login":"ace24713","id":753186,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzE4Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/753186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713","html_url":"https://github.com/ace24713","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T17:27:35Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T17:27:35Z","body":"I'm curious about how some of this works...\r\n> When a long press is detected, the original touch is canceled\r\n\r\nHow does that work? I see InputEventScreenTouch has a \"canceled\" property, but I don't see anywhere in base_button where it's actually checked, so I find it hard to believe it handles everything intently and is left in a good state in all cases. Call it a hunch.\r\n> When Action Mode = Button Release and Button Mask = Mouse Right ... A long press triggers a single button press action when the touch is released.\r\n\r\nThat's also curious. If it ignores emulated events, how does it even respond to the emulated right click? Are emulated right-click events not set as DEVICE_ID_EMULATION? I mean I guess that'd be fine as long as it works, it's just unexpected.\r\n> A normal tap always generates a press event.\r\n\r\nIf \"always\" in this context means even when Button Mask = Mouse Right, that sounds like another regression too. Before multitouch support, a button with Mouse Right would not respond to short taps, but would respond to long presses. (worth noting I didn't explicitly verify that, but it's sensible)\r\n> Button Mask = Mouse Right: A press action is triggered immediately on touch. If the touch is held long enough to become a long press, an additional press action is triggered for the right-click event.\r\n\r\nSimilarly to the above, this is probably not how it would have behaved before multitouch support.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886965206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887117281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962#issuecomment-4887117281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120962","id":4887117281,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0t94Q","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T18:20:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T18:20:25Z","body":"> > When a long press is detected, the original touch is canceled\r\n> \r\n> How does that work? I see InputEventScreenTouch has a \"canceled\" property, but I don't see anywhere in base_button where it's actually checked, so I find it hard to believe it handles everything intently and is left in a good state in all cases. Call it a hunch.\r\n\r\nCode checks for `!event->is_pressed()` which also handles canceled event. As you can see in the changes, where press action is triggered, I've now updated the check to `event->is_released()`, so it doesn't trigger a press for canceled events.\r\n\r\n> > When Action Mode = Button Release and Button Mask = Mouse Right ... A long press triggers a single button press action when the touch is released.\r\n> \r\n> That's also curious. If it ignores emulated events, how does it even respond to the emulated right click? Are emulated right-click events not set as DEVICE_ID_EMULATION? I mean I guess that'd be fine as long as it works, it's just unexpected.\r\n\r\nYes, right click generated by `enable_long_press_as_right_click` setting, does not have DEVICE_ID_EMULATION. These are like regular mouse click. DEVICE_ID_EMULATION is only being used for `emulate_touch_from_mouse` and `emulate_mouse_from_touch` setting. \r\n\r\n> > A normal tap always generates a press event.\r\n> \r\n> If \"always\" in this context means even when Button Mask = Mouse Right, that sounds like another regression too. Before multitouch support, a button with Mouse Right would not respond to short taps, but would respond to long presses. (worth noting I didn't explicitly verify that, but it's sensible)\r\n> \r\n> > Button Mask = Mouse Right: A press action is triggered immediately on touch. If the touch is held long enough to become a long press, an additional press action is triggered for the right-click event.\r\n> \r\n> Similarly to the above, this is probably not how it would have behaved before multitouch support.\r\n\r\nYes, button mask is ignored for touch input. This does sounds like a regression but I'm not sure what we can do here, you know touch have no concept of button mask.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4887117281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4889042368","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962#issuecomment-4889042368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120962","id":4889042368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI2jdwA","user":{"login":"ace24713","id":753186,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzE4Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/753186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713","html_url":"https://github.com/ace24713","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T04:20:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T04:20:34Z","body":"> Code checks for !event->is_pressed() which also handles canceled event. As you can see in the changes, where press action is triggered, I've now updated the check to event->is_released(), so it doesn't trigger a press for canceled events.\r\n\r\nOhh that makes sense, I was not aware that is_released is cancel aware. 👍\r\n\r\n> Yes, button mask is ignored for touch input. This does sounds like a regression but I'm not sure what we can do here, you know touch have no concept of button mask.\r\n\r\nIf I were to make a proposal...\r\n\r\nIn terms of regression minimization, I think treating touch inputs as left mouse events would be simple. That would be intuitive enough, I certainly wouldn't expect a touch input to be able to press a button coded to respond only to right mouse.\r\n\r\nAlternatively...\r\n\r\nWhat about adding \"touch\" as a potential mask option? That way buttons can be individually set to respond to whatever sorts of inputs the user wants. For example I could set a button to respond to mouse events only (which also works as a compatibility setting) or respond to touch and right mouse, touch and right and left mouse, or any combination.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4889042368/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4928467572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962#issuecomment-4928467572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120962","id":4928467572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJcJydA","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-09T18:49:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T18:49:15Z","body":"> What about adding \"touch\" as a potential mask option? That way buttons can be individually set to respond to whatever sorts of inputs the user wants. For example I could set a button to respond to mouse events only (which also works as a compatibility setting) or respond to touch and right mouse, touch and right and left mouse, or any combination.\r\n\r\nI personally like this option, but final call on this would be from `Input` or `GUI` team. It would be great if you can make a proposal with both of your suggestions.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4928467572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4932971701","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962#issuecomment-4932971701","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120962","id":4932971701,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJgcstQ","user":{"login":"ace24713","id":753186,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzE4Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/753186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713","html_ur